invariant: INV-17
file: gcm_avx512_kernel.h
catches: test/quic-builds.sh
reason: GCM_AVX512_BELOW_LEN, the bytes of stack gcm_avx512.c's entries wipe
  below their frames after each kernel call, is 1,024, less than the
  frames the kernel writes, so the wipe runs and still leaves the powers of
  the hash subkey where they lay. Every byte is right. The Makefile reads
  the length for the kernel's lint-stack ceiling, 512 bytes below it, and
  the script compiles the kernel for x86-64 under that ceiling, which its
  frames pass; bin/gcm_avx512_equiv_test measures the depth itself on a
  CPU with AVX-512.

--- old
#define GCM_AVX512_BELOW_LEN 2560
--- new
#define GCM_AVX512_BELOW_LEN 1024
